# Commit Message Template

## Commit Message Format

```xml
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

<body>

<footer>
```

## Types

- `feat`: New feature
- `fix`: Bug fix
- `docs`: Documentation changes
- `style`: Code style changes (formatting, etc.)
- `refactor`: Code refactoring
- `perf`: Performance improvements
- `test`: Adding or updating tests
- `chore`: Maintenance tasks (dependencies, build, etc.)
- `security`: Security-related changes

## Scope

Optional. Examples: `docker`, `nginx`, `dns`, `deps`, `ci`, etc.

## Subject

- Use imperative mood ("add" not "added" or "adds")
- First letter lowercase
- No period at the end
- Maximum 72 characters

## Body

Optional. Explain what and why, not how.

## Footer

Optional. Reference issues, breaking changes, etc.

## Important Reminders

- **Update DEPENDENCIES.md**: If you add, remove, or update any dependencies (Alpine `apk` packages or Python `pip` packages), you MUST update [DEPENDENCIES.md](DEPENDENCIES.md) to reflect the changes.

- **Version Pinning**: All dependencies must be pinned to exact versions for security. See [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) for details.

## Examples

```txt
feat(nginx): add PHP 8.2 support

Add PHP 8.2 packages to nginx container with version pinning.

- Update DEPENDENCIES.md with PHP 8.2 packages
```

```txt
chore(deps): update libtool to 2.4.7-r3

Update libtool version to fix build errors.

- Update DEPENDENCIES.md
```

```txt
fix(mailinabox): pin perl package versions

Fix version conflicts by updating perl packages to 5.38.5-r0.

- Update DEPENDENCIES.md with new perl versions
```
